      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\r\n- [X] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\r\n- [X] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\r\n\r\n### Electron Version\r\n\r\nnot sure, the app is not developed by myself.\r\n\r\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\r\n\r\nUbuntu\r\n\r\n### Operating System Version\r\n\r\nubuntu18.04\r\n\r\n### What arch are you using?\r\n\r\nx64\r\n\r\n### Last Known Working Electron version\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nFor some other GUI Apps, e.g., gedit and firefox, which are installed in the docker container, I can input Chinese correctly in their text-input panels. So I expect that I can also type Chinese in my Electron-based GUI App.\r\n\r\n### Actual Behavior\r\n\r\n Actually, I cannot type it. But the ibus property-panel can correctly display in the text-panel. I'm not sure it's a issue related to Electron, but it's really strange.\r\n\r\n### Testcase Gist URL\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Additional Information\r\n\r\n_No response_",
